        "name": "Methodical Debilitations",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>You strategically craft your debilitations to lessen or negate an enemy's tactical advantages. Add the following debilitations to the list you can choose from when you use Debilitating Strike.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Debilitation</strong> The target can't flank or contribute to allies' flanking. @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feat-effects.Item.Effect: Methodical Debilitations (Flanking)]</li>\n<li><strong>Debilitation</strong> The target doesn't gain a circumstance bonus to AC from @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Raise a Shield]{Raising a Shield}, lesser cover, or standard cover; it gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC only from greater cover or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Take Cover]{Taking Cover}. @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feat-effects.Item.Effect: Methodical Debilitations (Cover)]</li>\n</ul>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 10
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": [
              {
                "value": "mastermind racket"
              },
              {
                "value": "Debilitating Strike"
              }
            ]
          },
